From 19e91ac9d8a7f43e582192dad68c891a775e8004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaughanb <brenden.vaughan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:25:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] LiteNetLibManager: move a running client to another server
 and keep its objects

A client can now reconnect to another server without the client
teardown, and the objects it had on screen are kept and adopted by the
new server's spawns of the same objects instead of being destroyed and
instantiated again. Nothing changes for a game that does not call it.

- LiteNetLibManager.MigrateClient(address, port) reconnects the
  client's transport while IsClient and the logic updater keep running;
  the overload taking an ITransport continues on a transport that is
  connected to the new server already (opened ahead of time), so no
  connect round trip is spent. EndMigrateClient ends it;
  IsMigratingClient is true in between. LiteNetLibClient gains
  AdoptConnectedTransport for the second form.
- LiteNetLibGameManager keeps the client's spawned objects
  (LiteNetLibAssets.KeepSpawnedObjects) instead of destroying them, keeps
  the old connection id until the new server answers so owned objects
  stay owned and simulated, and rebinds their owner to the new
  connection id (RebindKeptObjectsOwner).
- LiteNetLibAssets.NetworkSpawn on a migrating client adopts the kept
  object a spawn is (ResolveKeptObject: same prefab and ownership, the
  owned one or the nearest within keptObjectAdoptDistance; or a
  keptObjectResolver) and raises onObjectAdopted with its previous id.
  DestroyKeptObjects removes what no spawn adopted. WarmUpAdoption runs
  the adoption read once ahead of time so it is not compiled in the
  frame of the first adoption.
- An adopted object's initial state is applied as a diff: a sync field
  fires its callbacks only for a value that differs, and a sync list is
  brought to the state it was sent with Set/Add/RemoveLast operations
  (entries compared in wire form) instead of Clear plus AddInitial, so
  listeners only hear about what changed (LiteNetLibElement.IsBeingAdopted,
  LiteNetLibIdentity.IsKept/IsBeingAdopted/AdoptedFromObjectId).
- On a client, an owner change for an object not spawned yet logs at
  dev level instead of warning: the owner message overtakes the spawn,
  and the spawn carries the owner.

Tests: KeptObjectAdoptionTests, PreconnectedMigrationTests (EditMode).

Used by a server-meshing add-on whose players walk between map-server
processes of one map with nothing on screen torn down at the crossing.
